[22:09:15] STORY-DOM-023 is complete. I resumed the interrupted attempt rather than restarting it.
[22:09:15] ## What was already on disk (verified, not rewritten)
[22:09:15] `tradingpost/TradingPostFeePolicy.java`, its test, the `CraftingPlanner` fee deduction, and the `CraftResult` field documentation. **Two defects in that work were found and fixed:**
[22:09:15] - its own test asserted `feeOn(10) == 1`, while 15% of 10c is 1.5c and the documented half-away-from-zero rule gives 2 — the implementation was right, the expectation was wrong;
[22:09:15] - the planner passed revenue to `feeOn` unguarded, so a stored output quote of zero or less would have thrown `IllegalArgumentException` out of the planner where the old code produced a negative profit the availability predicates then suppressed.
[22:09:15] ## What I added
[22:09:15] - **Domain:** a `revenueOne > 0` guard; new `CraftingPlannerProfitFeeTest` (8 cases: §25's own 300c/204c → 51c example, both sale modes, multi-output/multi-craft totals, purchased-material loss, break-even, unavailable and non-positive prices, and the small-copper case that separates §25's percentage model from §25.1's minimum-fee transaction model).
[22:09:15] - **Corrected, not weakened**, three existing expectations: 2 980/14 900 → 2 530/12 650, 80/160 → 65/130, 500 → 425 — each with gross revenue and total sell value asserted unchanged beside it.
[22:09:15] - **HTTP:** a new Discovery fresh-detail test pinning the row to mutually underivable values and asserting an unavailable result keeps all four money fields absent. Profit's table and fresh-detail passthrough was already covered.
[22:09:15] - **Browser:** `after 15% TP fees` on Profit and Total profit in the Profit detail, aligned in Discovery's shared detail; component tests plus a new `smoke:profit` step.
[22:09:15] - **JavaFX:** replaced the now-false `GW2 TradingFees will still be deducted -15%!` tooltip and stated the fee in both profit tooltips; a new TestFX case reads the real table and the header tooltips back.
[22:09:15] - **Docs:** `CURRENT_STATE_SPEC.md` §15, four places in `CURRENT_ARCHITECTURE.md`, `KNOWN_PROBLEMS.md` KP-09's stale sentence, and the §35 crafting guide (fee section, formula, worked example, FAQ entry).
[22:09:15] ## Tests (all real output, `BUILD SUCCESS`)
[22:09:15] 28 domain, 51 planner-dependent, 87 HTTP/presentation, 213 frontend unit, `smoke:profit` 38 steps, `smoke:discovery` 13 steps, `CraftingProfitViewSmokeIT` 2/2 on a real desktop and disposable Postgres schema.
[22:09:15] ## Limits worth your attention
[22:09:15] No live-data run — browser evidence is controlled-response only. Half-away-from-zero rounding is a project convention, not verified game behaviour. Ectoplasm still uses its own 15% multiplier (DOM-024), and `TradingPostSaleCalculator` still has no caller, as §25.1 requires. **No Phase 5 performance or completion claim.**
[22:09:15] Two follow-up findings recorded (`F001`: `CostEvaluationResult`'s unread pre-fee profit fields now contradict §26; `F002`: JavaFX derives Total sell value in the view rather than carrying the domain's figure). I did not commit or push.
